---
source: crates/wn-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: help(path)
---
Fast local "where next" hints for coding agents and developers

Usage: wn [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init       Index the repository and fit its personal adapter from git history
  setup      Connect Claude Code, Codex and Cursor so hints reach them automatically (skill + hooks)
  ask        Rank the files (and optionally functions) to open next for a task
  status     Show the index, coverage and adapter state
  train      Refit the personal adapter now
  rollback   Restore the previous adapter (or remove the only one)
  mcp        Serve hints over MCP (stdio)
  bench      Measure hit@k on this repository's own history (default) or on ContextBench
  update     Update release installs from the latest release; rebuild source installs from main (or --ref)
  report     Share an anonymous usage report as a GitHub issue (shown first; asks before sending)
  stats      How wn is doing: whether agents acted on its hints, a replay against grep, speed
  daemon     Start, stop or inspect the background daemon that keeps models and indexes warm
  skill      The where-next skill (`wn skill sync` is `wn setup`; `wn skill show` prints it)
  uninstall  Remove wn and everything it added: agent skill and hooks, caches, models, the binary
  model      Install, list or remove models
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          Repository (or any directory inside it), or a directory of repositories
          
          [default: .]

      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

      --model <MODEL>
          Model directory (default: `$WN_MODEL_DIR`, else the best installed model)

      --no-daemon
          Answer in this process instead of the background daemon (also `WN_NO_DAEMON=1`)

      --any-dir
          Allow a directory outside any git repository, or your home directory or / itself (refused by default: everything under it would be indexed)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color text output: auto (terminal only; honors NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE), always or never
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  wn model pull                            install the default model (once, ~1.2 GB)
  wn init                                  index this repository, fit its adapter from git history
  wn status                                which model answers ("lexical fallback" = no model installed)
  wn ask "where is the retry logic for S3 upload timeouts"
  wn bench                                 replay this repository's history: hit@1/3/10
  wn stats                                 did your agents use the hints? replay vs grep, speed
  wn setup                                 connect Claude Code / Codex / Cursor (skill + hooks)

Docs: https://github.com/andreylukin/where-next#quick-start
